## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)

- “TWD 1.57M” is not an Icelandic spelling error to fix in this lane. A test and ACCEPTED-ROUND pin that byte string. The German “1,57 Millionen” hint does not apply.
- Q16 through the close are body lines in the English and Korean sources, not missing headings. Turning them into `##` headings would fail the heading-level check. The U+200B blanks, including lines that are only that character and the empty `**​**` lines in 005, are in the Korean source; deleting them fails the ZWSP count. The real prose defect in 008 and 009 (lines with no finite verb) was fixed inside the existing blocks.
- “(10)” on the 004 dividend-rule link is a bad article number for flno=3, as the reviewer says. It is also the digit the checker still counts from Korean “제10조” on that same link. Dropping it fails the file. The digit stays.
- “í 1 mánuð” in 002 and 008 is the Korean “1개월”, not a spare digit glued onto a word. “1 mánuð” in 013 was kept on purpose and only given “til viðbótar”.
- No gender change for Wei Tseng. The reviewer’s own verdict is right: “lögmaður” stays the ordinary Icelandic title, grammatically masculine, for a woman lawyer. “Hún” is already used where the pronoun is marked.
